{"timestamp":1774885478950,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"7b68532c-999b-4b71-b2c2-e5199cb05c08","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xud8zrGx4W1UA2tV1d3bRz","payload":{"session_id":"7b68532c-999b-4b71-b2c2-e5199cb05c08","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-1623864e/7b68532c-999b-4b71-b2c2-e5199cb05c08.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/1623864e","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/specs/patch/patch-adw-11-remove-ineffective-private-field-stub.md","content":"# Patch: Remove ineffective Python-style private field stub\n\n## Metadata\nadw_id: `11`\nreview_change_request: `sandbox.stub(repository, '_MasRepository__addToCache') uses Python-style name mangling which does not apply to JS # private fields. The stub silently no-ops, so #addToCache executes in the test; errors are caught by the try/catch so assertions still pass, but test isolation intent is not achieved. Resolution: Remove the ineffective stub and rely on the catch block for downstream errors, or refactor the method to accept a DI seam. Severity: tech_debt`\n\n## Issue Summary\n**Original Spec:** n/a\n**Issue:** Line 1521 in `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` calls `sandbox.stub(repository, '_MasRepository__addToCache')`. JavaScript private fields (`#addToCache`) are not reachable via Python-style name mangling (`_ClassName__method`) \u2014 the stub installs a dead property on the instance while the real `#addToCache` still executes. Errors from `#addToCache` (e.g. `initFragmentCache` not initialised in unit context) are silently swallowed by the surrounding `try/catch`, so test assertions still pass, but test isolation is not achieved and the stub comment is misleading.\n**Solution:** Remove the two lines that reference `_MasRepository__addToCache` (the stub call at line 1521 and the comment at line 1519 that refers to it). The `try/catch` blocks in each `it` block already handle downstream errors from the real `#addToCache`, so the tests continue to validate title-deduplication logic correctly without the dead stub.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`\n\n## Implementation Steps\nIMPORTANT: Execute every step in order, top to bottom.\n\n### Step 1: Remove the dead stub and its misleading comment\nIn `buildRepository()` inside the `'copyFragment title deduplication'` describe block, delete these two lines (currently at lines 1519\u20131521):\n\n```js\n// stub downstream methods to keep the test focused on title logic\nsandbox.stub(repository, 'processError');\nsandbox.stub(repository, '_MasRepository__addToCache').resolves({ id: 'new-id' });\n```\n\nReplace with (keep only the `processError` stub; drop the `_MasRepository__addToCache` stub and update the comment):\n\n```js\n// stub processError so caught errors don't surface as test noise\nsandbox.stub(repository, 'processError');\n```\n\nAlso remove the inline comment on line 1528 (`// Patch #addToCache and downstream via direct method stub`) inside the first `it` block, as it no longer applies.\n\n### Step 2: Verify the remaining `processError` stub is sufficient\nThe two `it` blocks already wrap `copyFragment` in `try { \u2026 } catch { /* \u2026 */ }`. The `#addToCache` call will still throw in the unit context (no `initFragmentCache`), but that error propagates to the `catch` block, which swallows it. The `save` spy check in the first test is done **before** `#addToCache` is reached (it is called after `save`), so assertion integrity is preserved.\n\nNo other changes are required.\n\n## Validation\nExecute every command to validate the patch is complete with zero regressions.\n\n1. Syntax check the modified file:\n   ```\n   node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js\n   ```\n\n2. Run the unit tests for `mas-repository`:\n   ```\n   cd /Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/1623864e && npm run test:unit 2>&1 | grep -E \"passing|failing|copyFragment\"\n   ```\n   Expected: all tests pass, no new failures.\n\n3. Confirm the dead stub is gone:\n   ```\n   grep -n '_MasRepository__addToCache' studio/test/mas-repository.test.js\n   ```\n   Expected: no output.\n\n## Patch Scope\n**Lines of code to change:** ~3 lines removed\n**Risk level:** low\n**Testing required:** Run the existing unit-test suite; the two `copyFragment title deduplication` tests must still pass.\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xud8zrGx4W1UA2tV1d3bRz"}}
